1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,248
Have you ever been

2
00:00:01,248 --> 00:00:02,300
one phone call away

3
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:03,187
from walking out

4
00:00:03,187 --> 00:00:04,240
on your whole life?

5
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:05,387
I was.

6
00:00:05,387 --> 00:00:06,861
Two in the morning,

7
00:00:06,861 --> 00:00:08,024
at a truck stop

8
00:00:08,024 --> 00:00:09,420
at the bottom of a

9
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:11,126
mountain in Tennessee.

10
00:00:11,126 --> 00:00:13,108
I'd written my resignation

11
00:00:13,108 --> 00:00:14,480
on a paper napkin.

12
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:15,299
Four words.

13
00:00:15,299 --> 00:00:15,896
Marlene.

14
00:00:15,896 --> 00:00:16,417
I quit.

15
00:00:16,417 --> 00:00:16,790
Hank.

16
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:18,620
I had a pocket full

17
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:20,106
of quarters, and I called

18
00:00:20,106 --> 00:00:21,413
the one man I was sure

19
00:00:21,413 --> 00:00:22,780
would be ashamed of me.

20
00:00:23,480 --> 00:00:24,436
My father listened

21
00:00:24,436 --> 00:00:25,392
to the whole thing

22
00:00:25,392 --> 00:00:26,560
without saying a word.

23
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,571
Then he said, "Son.

24
00:00:28,571 --> 00:00:30,241
Before you do anything,

25
00:00:30,241 --> 00:00:31,330
I want you to—"

26
00:00:32,030 --> 00:00:32,607
Hey.

27
00:00:32,607 --> 00:00:34,050
It's Hank.

28
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:36,049
Tonight I'm parked

29
00:00:36,049 --> 00:00:37,852
outside Laramie, Wyoming.

30
00:00:37,852 --> 00:00:39,050
I made it across.

31
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:40,365
And yes, I flashed

32
00:00:40,365 --> 00:00:42,118
my lights at that dip by

33
00:00:42,118 --> 00:00:43,653
Elk Mountain, the way

34
00:00:43,653 --> 00:00:45,042
I told you I would.

35
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:46,523
Nothing blinked back.

36
00:00:46,523 --> 00:00:47,249
I'll admit

37
00:00:47,249 --> 00:00:48,990
I was a little relieved.

38
00:00:49,690 --> 00:00:51,539
Last time was a hard one.

39
00:00:51,539 --> 00:00:53,167
Tonight's a quiet one.

40
00:00:53,167 --> 00:00:54,080
No blizzard,

41
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:55,755
no strange headlights.

42
00:00:55,755 --> 00:00:57,042
Just a pay phone,

43
00:00:57,042 --> 00:00:59,010
a mountain, and my father.

44
00:00:59,710 --> 00:01:00,650
Pull up a chair.

45
00:01:01,350 --> 00:01:02,427
It was Tuesday,

46
00:01:02,427 --> 00:01:03,862
April twenty-second,

47
00:01:03,862 --> 00:01:05,226
two thousand three.

48
00:01:05,226 --> 00:01:06,388
I was twenty-six

49
00:01:06,388 --> 00:01:07,114
years old,

50
00:01:07,114 --> 00:01:09,003
five years into long haul,

51
00:01:09,003 --> 00:01:10,579
and I hadn't been home

52
00:01:10,579 --> 00:01:11,940
in thirty-six days.

53
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,827
I had forty-three

54
00:01:13,827 --> 00:01:15,642
thousand pounds of roofing

55
00:01:15,642 --> 00:01:16,968
shingles behind me,

56
00:01:16,968 --> 00:01:18,418
Nashville to Atlanta,

57
00:01:18,418 --> 00:01:20,213
on Interstate twenty-four.

58
00:01:20,213 --> 00:01:21,047
Due at eight

59
00:01:21,047 --> 00:01:22,090
in the morning.

60
00:01:22,790 --> 00:01:24,085
Three days before,

61
00:01:24,085 --> 00:01:24,948
on Saturday,

62
00:01:24,948 --> 00:01:26,315
my boy turned five.

63
00:01:26,315 --> 00:01:27,144
I missed it.

64
00:01:27,144 --> 00:01:28,951
A load in Texas went bad,

65
00:01:28,951 --> 00:01:29,819
the receiver

66
00:01:29,819 --> 00:01:31,192
wouldn't unload me,

67
00:01:31,192 --> 00:01:32,976
and by the time they did,

68
00:01:32,976 --> 00:01:34,332
the party was over.

69
00:01:34,332 --> 00:01:35,615
I called the house

70
00:01:35,615 --> 00:01:36,970
that afternoon from

71
00:01:36,970 --> 00:01:38,824
a truck stop in Texarkana.

72
00:01:38,824 --> 00:01:40,673
My wife held the phone out

73
00:01:40,673 --> 00:01:42,522
to him, and I heard him in

74
00:01:42,522 --> 00:01:43,610
the background,

75
00:01:43,610 --> 00:01:44,989
with all his little

76
00:01:44,989 --> 00:01:46,150
friends yelling.

77
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:47,765
He said, "Mommy,

78
00:01:47,765 --> 00:01:48,680
it's the truck."

79
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:50,570
Not Daddy.

80
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:51,760
The truck.

81
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:53,428
He didn't mean

82
00:01:53,428 --> 00:01:54,465
anything by it.

83
00:01:54,465 --> 00:01:55,267
He was five.

84
00:01:55,267 --> 00:01:57,056
To him, I was a voice that

85
00:01:57,056 --> 00:01:58,707
came out of the phone on

86
00:01:58,707 --> 00:01:59,896
Sundays and a big

87
00:01:59,896 --> 00:02:01,366
noise in the driveway

88
00:02:01,366 --> 00:02:02,485
every few weeks.

89
00:02:02,485 --> 00:02:03,531
But I sat there

90
00:02:03,531 --> 00:02:04,785
in that truck stop

91
00:02:04,785 --> 00:02:06,598
with the phone in my hand,

92
00:02:06,598 --> 00:02:07,511
and something

93
00:02:07,511 --> 00:02:08,846
in me cracked right

94
00:02:08,846 --> 00:02:09,970
down the middle.

95
00:02:10,670 --> 00:02:11,733
My father drove

96
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:13,291
a truck my whole life.

97
00:02:13,291 --> 00:02:14,463
A green Kenworth.

98
00:02:14,463 --> 00:02:15,467
And I couldn't

99
00:02:15,467 --> 00:02:16,685
remember him ever

100
00:02:16,685 --> 00:02:18,119
missing my birthday.

101
00:02:18,119 --> 00:02:18,740
Not once.

102
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:19,954
I couldn't figure

103
00:02:19,954 --> 00:02:21,240
out how he did it,

104
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,740
and I couldn't do it.

105
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:24,708
Now, to understand what

106
00:02:24,708 --> 00:02:25,811
happened that night,

107
00:02:25,811 --> 00:02:26,693
you need to know

108
00:02:26,693 --> 00:02:27,630
about a mountain.

109
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:29,510
Between Nashville

110
00:02:29,510 --> 00:02:30,620
and Chattanooga,

111
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:31,321
Interstate

112
00:02:31,321 --> 00:02:32,792
twenty-four goes over

113
00:02:32,792 --> 00:02:34,123
Monteagle Mountain.

114
00:02:34,123 --> 00:02:35,888
If you drive a car, you've

115
00:02:35,888 --> 00:02:37,652
probably never noticed it.

116
00:02:37,652 --> 00:02:39,085
If you drive a truck,

117
00:02:39,085 --> 00:02:40,449
you know it by name.

118
00:02:40,449 --> 00:02:41,838
It's one of the most

119
00:02:41,838 --> 00:02:42,741
famous grades

120
00:02:42,741 --> 00:02:43,782
in the country,

121
00:02:43,782 --> 00:02:45,310
and not in a good way.

122
00:02:46,010 --> 00:02:47,494
Here's the thing about

123
00:02:47,494 --> 00:02:48,844
a loaded truck going

124
00:02:48,844 --> 00:02:49,923
down a mountain.

125
00:02:49,923 --> 00:02:50,668
Your brakes

126
00:02:50,668 --> 00:02:51,684
are not enough.

127
00:02:51,684 --> 00:02:53,296
They're drums and shoes,

128
00:02:53,296 --> 00:02:54,773
and every time you use

129
00:02:54,773 --> 00:02:56,250
them, they get hotter.

130
00:02:56,250 --> 00:02:57,593
Get them hot enough,

131
00:02:57,593 --> 00:02:58,533
and they fade.

132
00:02:58,533 --> 00:02:59,895
The pedal goes soft,

133
00:02:59,895 --> 00:03:01,120
the smell comes up

134
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:02,346
through the floor,

135
00:03:02,346 --> 00:03:03,974
like burnt toast and hot

136
00:03:03,974 --> 00:03:05,467
pennies, and the truck

137
00:03:05,467 --> 00:03:06,620
just keeps going.

138
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:08,427
So you don't use

139
00:03:08,427 --> 00:03:09,602
your brakes to go

140
00:03:09,602 --> 00:03:10,709
down a mountain.

141
00:03:10,709 --> 00:03:12,038
You use your engine.

142
00:03:12,038 --> 00:03:13,340
You pick a low gear

143
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:14,985
at the top, and you turn

144
00:03:14,985 --> 00:03:16,424
on your engine brake.

145
00:03:16,424 --> 00:03:18,018
Truckers call it a Jake.

146
00:03:18,018 --> 00:03:19,467
It's that loud rattle

147
00:03:19,467 --> 00:03:20,640
you hear from big

148
00:03:20,640 --> 00:03:22,427
trucks coming down a hill,

149
00:03:22,427 --> 00:03:23,733
like a machine gun.

150
00:03:23,733 --> 00:03:25,520
The engine holds you back,

151
00:03:25,520 --> 00:03:26,483
and the brakes

152
00:03:26,483 --> 00:03:27,720
are just for help.

153
00:03:28,420 --> 00:03:29,847
And there's one rule

154
00:03:29,847 --> 00:03:31,202
every driver learns

155
00:03:31,202 --> 00:03:32,272
his first year.

156
00:03:32,272 --> 00:03:33,553
You pick your gear

157
00:03:33,553 --> 00:03:34,336
at the top.

158
00:03:34,336 --> 00:03:35,630
Because if you try

159
00:03:35,630 --> 00:03:36,996
to shift on the way

160
00:03:36,996 --> 00:03:38,505
down and you miss it,

161
00:03:38,505 --> 00:03:39,791
even for a second,

162
00:03:39,791 --> 00:03:41,077
you're in neutral.

163
00:03:41,077 --> 00:03:41,764
No engine.

164
00:03:41,764 --> 00:03:43,119
Forty tons, rolling

165
00:03:43,119 --> 00:03:44,687
downhill, with nothing

166
00:03:44,687 --> 00:03:46,184
holding it but brakes

167
00:03:46,184 --> 00:03:47,680
that are already hot.

168
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:49,831
That's why mountains

169
00:03:49,831 --> 00:03:51,209
have runaway ramps.

170
00:03:51,209 --> 00:03:52,606
Long lanes of deep,

171
00:03:52,606 --> 00:03:53,562
loose gravel,

172
00:03:53,562 --> 00:03:55,033
running off the side

173
00:03:55,033 --> 00:03:56,725
of the road and uphill.

174
00:03:56,725 --> 00:03:58,473
If your brakes are gone,

175
00:03:58,473 --> 00:04:00,367
you steer into the gravel,

176
00:04:00,367 --> 00:04:01,257
and it grabs

177
00:04:01,257 --> 00:04:02,890
your wheels and buries

178
00:04:02,890 --> 00:04:04,151
you to the axles.

179
00:04:04,151 --> 00:04:06,037
It's ugly, it's expensive,

180
00:04:06,037 --> 00:04:06,980
and you live.

181
00:04:07,680 --> 00:04:09,348
There's an old saying.

182
00:04:09,348 --> 00:04:11,357
You can go down a mountain

183
00:04:11,357 --> 00:04:13,366
too slow a thousand times.

184
00:04:13,366 --> 00:04:14,537
You can only go

185
00:04:14,537 --> 00:04:16,020
down too fast once.

186
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,518
On the way down Monteagle,

187
00:04:18,518 --> 00:04:19,556
there's a sign.

188
00:04:19,556 --> 00:04:20,184
Truckers,

189
00:04:20,184 --> 00:04:21,650
you are not down yet.

190
00:04:22,350 --> 00:04:23,942
I passed it that night

191
00:04:23,942 --> 00:04:25,679
at about eleven o'clock.

192
00:04:25,679 --> 00:04:27,450
And I was going too fast.

193
00:04:28,150 --> 00:04:28,947
I was late.

194
00:04:28,947 --> 00:04:30,614
I'd been late all week.

195
00:04:30,614 --> 00:04:32,097
I was tired in a way

196
00:04:32,097 --> 00:04:33,803
that sleep doesn't fix.

197
00:04:33,803 --> 00:04:35,651
And I did the thing every

198
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:37,572
old-timer warns you about.

199
00:04:37,572 --> 00:04:39,000
I went over the top

200
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:40,428
in too high a gear,

201
00:04:40,428 --> 00:04:42,232
telling myself I'd catch

202
00:04:42,232 --> 00:04:43,660
it on the way down.

203
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,193
Halfway down,

204
00:04:45,193 --> 00:04:46,730
I knew I was in trouble.

205
00:04:47,430 --> 00:04:48,973
The truck was gaining.

206
00:04:48,973 --> 00:04:49,393
Fifty.

207
00:04:49,393 --> 00:04:50,164
Fifty-five.

208
00:04:50,164 --> 00:04:51,470
I had the Jake on,

209
00:04:51,470 --> 00:04:52,848
and it was roaring,

210
00:04:52,848 --> 00:04:54,371
and it wasn't enough.

211
00:04:54,371 --> 00:04:56,158
I touched the brakes, and

212
00:04:56,158 --> 00:04:58,017
I smelled them right away.

213
00:04:58,017 --> 00:04:58,859
Burnt toast.

214
00:04:58,859 --> 00:04:59,700
Hot pennies.

215
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,071
I had to get a lower gear.

216
00:05:02,071 --> 00:05:03,659
And there's no way to do

217
00:05:03,659 --> 00:05:05,114
that on a hill without

218
00:05:05,114 --> 00:05:06,570
going through neutral.

219
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:08,800
So I pushed in the clutch,

220
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,506
and I pulled

221
00:05:09,506 --> 00:05:10,800
the stick out of gear,

222
00:05:10,800 --> 00:05:11,910
and for one second,

223
00:05:11,910 --> 00:05:13,020
the truck was free.

224
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:14,832
You can feel it.

225
00:05:14,832 --> 00:05:16,265
Forty-three thousand

226
00:05:16,265 --> 00:05:17,627
pounds of shingles,

227
00:05:17,627 --> 00:05:19,418
and nothing holding them.

228
00:05:19,418 --> 00:05:20,427
Just the hill,

229
00:05:20,427 --> 00:05:21,941
and the dark, and the

230
00:05:21,941 --> 00:05:23,310
sound of the tires.

231
00:05:24,010 --> 00:05:25,360
I went for the lower gear,

232
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:26,190
and I missed it.

233
00:05:26,890 --> 00:05:27,987
The stick ground

234
00:05:27,987 --> 00:05:29,152
against the gears

235
00:05:29,152 --> 00:05:30,729
and bounced back at me.

236
00:05:30,729 --> 00:05:31,751
The speedometer

237
00:05:31,751 --> 00:05:33,046
climbed past sixty.

238
00:05:33,046 --> 00:05:34,748
And I'll tell you exactly

239
00:05:34,748 --> 00:05:36,178
what I thought about,

240
00:05:36,178 --> 00:05:37,812
because it surprised me.

241
00:05:37,812 --> 00:05:38,362
I didn't

242
00:05:38,362 --> 00:05:39,599
think about dying.

243
00:05:39,599 --> 00:05:40,767
I thought, my boy

244
00:05:40,767 --> 00:05:42,141
is going to remember

245
00:05:42,141 --> 00:05:43,240
me as the truck.

246
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:44,912
I tried again.

247
00:05:44,912 --> 00:05:46,361
I matched the engine

248
00:05:46,361 --> 00:05:47,738
to the road the way

249
00:05:47,738 --> 00:05:49,115
my father taught me

250
00:05:49,115 --> 00:05:50,494
when I was sixteen,

251
00:05:50,494 --> 00:05:51,582
in a hay field,

252
00:05:51,582 --> 00:05:53,178
in his green Kenworth.

253
00:05:53,178 --> 00:05:54,637
And the gear went in.

254
00:05:54,637 --> 00:05:55,871
The engine caught

255
00:05:55,871 --> 00:05:57,396
the truck like a hand

256
00:05:57,396 --> 00:05:58,558
catching a ball,

257
00:05:58,558 --> 00:06:00,002
and the Jake started

258
00:06:00,002 --> 00:06:01,806
hammering, and the needle

259
00:06:01,806 --> 00:06:03,250
started coming down.

260
00:06:03,950 --> 00:06:05,184
Fifty-five.

261
00:06:05,184 --> 00:06:05,856
Fifty.

262
00:06:05,856 --> 00:06:07,090
Forty-five.

263
00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:08,979
And then my headlights

264
00:06:08,979 --> 00:06:10,277
swept across the runaway

265
00:06:10,277 --> 00:06:11,250
ramp on the right.

266
00:06:11,950 --> 00:06:12,778
There was already

267
00:06:12,778 --> 00:06:13,460
a truck in it.

268
00:06:14,160 --> 00:06:15,734
A big red tractor with

269
00:06:15,734 --> 00:06:17,379
a flatbed, buried up to

270
00:06:17,379 --> 00:06:19,165
its fuel tanks in gravel,

271
00:06:19,165 --> 00:06:20,808
its four-ways blinking.

272
00:06:20,808 --> 00:06:22,462
The driver was standing

273
00:06:22,462 --> 00:06:24,115
next to it in the cold,

274
00:06:24,115 --> 00:06:25,553
smoking a cigarette,

275
00:06:25,553 --> 00:06:27,285
and his hand was shaking

276
00:06:27,285 --> 00:06:28,583
so bad I could see

277
00:06:28,583 --> 00:06:29,810
it from the road.

278
00:06:30,510 --> 00:06:32,252
That was going to be me.

279
00:06:32,252 --> 00:06:33,817
One more missed gear,

280
00:06:33,817 --> 00:06:35,010
and that was me.

281
00:06:35,710 --> 00:06:37,157
I made it to the bottom

282
00:06:37,157 --> 00:06:38,666
at thirty miles an hour,

283
00:06:38,666 --> 00:06:40,113
with my brakes smoking,

284
00:06:40,113 --> 00:06:41,196
and I pulled into

285
00:06:41,196 --> 00:06:42,470
the first truck stop

286
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:43,681
I saw, and I parked

287
00:06:43,681 --> 00:06:44,700
in the back row,

288
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:46,281
and I sat there with both

289
00:06:46,281 --> 00:06:47,418
hands on the wheel

290
00:06:47,418 --> 00:06:48,430
for a long time.

291
00:06:49,130 --> 00:06:50,390
Then I went inside.

292
00:06:51,090 --> 00:06:51,970
It was almost

293
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:53,257
two in the morning.

294
00:06:53,257 --> 00:06:54,999
A waitress was mopping the

295
00:06:54,999 --> 00:06:56,540
floor under the stools.

296
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:57,710
I sat in a booth,

297
00:06:57,710 --> 00:06:59,086
and I ordered coffee

298
00:06:59,086 --> 00:07:00,118
I didn't drink,

299
00:07:00,118 --> 00:07:01,559
and I pulled a napkin

300
00:07:01,559 --> 00:07:02,725
out of the holder

301
00:07:02,725 --> 00:07:03,960
and I wrote on it.

302
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:05,616
Marlene.

303
00:07:05,616 --> 00:07:06,452
I quit.

304
00:07:06,452 --> 00:07:07,050
Hank.

305
00:07:07,750 --> 00:07:09,553
Marlene was my dispatcher

306
00:07:09,553 --> 00:07:10,274
back then.

307
00:07:10,274 --> 00:07:11,894
She'd been dispatching

308
00:07:11,894 --> 00:07:12,778
trucks since

309
00:07:12,778 --> 00:07:14,104
before I was born,

310
00:07:14,104 --> 00:07:15,129
and she called

311
00:07:15,129 --> 00:07:16,373
every driver hon.

312
00:07:16,373 --> 00:07:16,955
I'd tell

313
00:07:16,955 --> 00:07:18,336
her in the morning.

314
00:07:18,336 --> 00:07:20,162
I'd deliver the shingles,

315
00:07:20,162 --> 00:07:21,112
and I'd quit,

316
00:07:21,112 --> 00:07:22,646
and I'd find a job in

317
00:07:22,646 --> 00:07:24,249
Ohio where I came home

318
00:07:24,249 --> 00:07:25,852
every night and nobody

319
00:07:25,852 --> 00:07:27,310
called me the truck.

320
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:29,510
I had it all figured out.

321
00:07:30,210 --> 00:07:31,777
My cell phone was dead.

322
00:07:31,777 --> 00:07:33,174
I'd left the charger

323
00:07:33,174 --> 00:07:34,570
in a motel in Texas.

324
00:07:34,570 --> 00:07:36,390
So I went to the pay phone

325
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:37,860
by the restrooms with

326
00:07:37,860 --> 00:07:39,680
a pocket full of quarters.

327
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,928
I didn't call my wife.

328
00:07:41,928 --> 00:07:43,299
I want to be honest

329
00:07:43,299 --> 00:07:44,671
with you about why.

330
00:07:44,671 --> 00:07:45,828
If I called her,

331
00:07:45,828 --> 00:07:47,274
she'd say come home.

332
00:07:47,274 --> 00:07:48,785
And I wanted somebody

333
00:07:48,785 --> 00:07:50,440
to tell me I was wrong.

334
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,073
Or right.

335
00:07:51,073 --> 00:07:52,480
I didn't know which.

336
00:07:53,180 --> 00:07:54,500
So I called my father.

337
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:56,010
He picked up

338
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:57,226
on the first ring.

339
00:07:57,226 --> 00:07:58,664
At two in the morning.

340
00:07:58,664 --> 00:07:59,710
He said, "Hank."

341
00:08:00,410 --> 00:08:01,259
Not hello.

342
00:08:01,259 --> 00:08:02,363
Just my name.

343
00:08:02,363 --> 00:08:03,155
Like he'd

344
00:08:03,155 --> 00:08:04,740
been expecting me.

345
00:08:05,440 --> 00:08:07,239
And I told him everything.

346
00:08:07,239 --> 00:08:08,139
The birthday.

347
00:08:08,139 --> 00:08:08,831
The truck.

348
00:08:08,831 --> 00:08:09,730
The mountain.

349
00:08:09,730 --> 00:08:10,837
The missed gear.

350
00:08:10,837 --> 00:08:12,324
The ramp, and the man

351
00:08:12,324 --> 00:08:13,882
with the shaking hand.

352
00:08:13,882 --> 00:08:14,920
And the napkin.

353
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:16,861
He didn't say a word

354
00:08:16,861 --> 00:08:17,791
the whole time.

355
00:08:17,791 --> 00:08:19,160
I could hear the clock

356
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:20,528
in my mother's kitchen

357
00:08:20,528 --> 00:08:21,710
ticking behind him.

358
00:08:22,410 --> 00:08:23,626
When I was done,

359
00:08:23,626 --> 00:08:24,843
I waited for it.

360
00:08:24,843 --> 00:08:26,651
My father had never been

361
00:08:26,651 --> 00:08:28,383
late a day in his life.

362
00:08:28,383 --> 00:08:29,601
I waited for him

363
00:08:29,601 --> 00:08:31,276
to tell me I was soft,

364
00:08:31,276 --> 00:08:33,103
or that I'd made my bed.

365
00:08:33,103 --> 00:08:34,430
I'd have taken it.

366
00:08:35,130 --> 00:08:36,720
Instead, he said, "Okay."

367
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:39,827
That was all, for a while.

368
00:08:39,827 --> 00:08:40,290
Okay.

369
00:08:40,990 --> 00:08:42,274
Then he said, "Son.

370
00:08:42,274 --> 00:08:43,996
Before you do anything, I

371
00:08:43,996 --> 00:08:45,719
want you to listen to me.

372
00:08:45,719 --> 00:08:47,340
Two in the morning lies.

373
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,151
You hear me?

374
00:08:48,151 --> 00:08:49,826
Two in the morning lies,

375
00:08:49,826 --> 00:08:51,362
and so does the bottom

376
00:08:51,362 --> 00:08:52,339
of a mountain.

377
00:08:52,339 --> 00:08:53,461
Nobody ever made

378
00:08:53,461 --> 00:08:54,512
a good decision

379
00:08:54,512 --> 00:08:56,054
at two in the morning.

380
00:08:56,054 --> 00:08:57,443
Go out to your truck

381
00:08:57,443 --> 00:08:58,554
and go to sleep.

382
00:08:58,554 --> 00:09:00,292
If you still want to quit

383
00:09:00,292 --> 00:09:01,543
when the sun's up,

384
00:09:01,543 --> 00:09:03,350
I'll come get you myself."

385
00:09:04,050 --> 00:09:04,796
I laughed.

386
00:09:04,796 --> 00:09:06,214
I couldn't help it.

387
00:09:06,214 --> 00:09:07,669
He was four hundred

388
00:09:07,669 --> 00:09:09,200
miles away, in Ohio.

389
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:10,658
I said, "Dad,

390
00:09:10,658 --> 00:09:12,000
you can't come get me."

391
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:13,379
And he said,

392
00:09:13,379 --> 00:09:14,510
"Go to sleep, Hank."

393
00:09:15,210 --> 00:09:16,160
And he hung up.

394
00:09:16,860 --> 00:09:17,431
So let me

395
00:09:17,431 --> 00:09:18,573
ask you something.

396
00:09:18,573 --> 00:09:20,093
And I want you to really

397
00:09:20,093 --> 00:09:20,980
think about it

398
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:22,120
before you answer.

399
00:09:22,820 --> 00:09:23,611
If it was two

400
00:09:23,611 --> 00:09:24,523
in the morning,

401
00:09:24,523 --> 00:09:25,679
and you were at the

402
00:09:25,679 --> 00:09:26,775
bottom of your own

403
00:09:26,775 --> 00:09:27,323
mountain,

404
00:09:27,323 --> 00:09:28,480
who would you call?

405
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:29,577
Not who you'd text.

406
00:09:29,577 --> 00:09:30,885
Who would you actually

407
00:09:30,885 --> 00:09:32,074
call, knowing they'd

408
00:09:32,074 --> 00:09:33,620
pick up on the first ring?

409
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:35,378
Some of you have

410
00:09:35,378 --> 00:09:36,766
an answer right away.

411
00:09:36,766 --> 00:09:37,925
Some of you don't.

412
00:09:37,925 --> 00:09:38,890
I've been both.

413
00:09:39,590 --> 00:09:41,253
I went out to my truck.

414
00:09:41,253 --> 00:09:42,884
I lay down in the bunk

415
00:09:42,884 --> 00:09:44,144
with my boots on.

416
00:09:44,144 --> 00:09:46,024
I thought I'd never sleep.

417
00:09:46,024 --> 00:09:46,773
I was gone

418
00:09:46,773 --> 00:09:48,120
in about a minute.

419
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:49,674
When I woke up,

420
00:09:49,674 --> 00:09:50,698
the sun was coming

421
00:09:50,698 --> 00:09:51,836
through the curtain,

422
00:09:51,836 --> 00:09:52,968
and it was a quarter

423
00:09:52,968 --> 00:09:53,590
after nine.

424
00:09:54,290 --> 00:09:55,691
And there was a sound

425
00:09:55,691 --> 00:09:56,825
outside I'd known

426
00:09:56,825 --> 00:09:57,759
my whole life.

427
00:09:57,759 --> 00:09:59,473
A big diesel, idling, with

428
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:01,122
a little lope in it, like

429
00:10:01,122 --> 00:10:02,770
it was humming to itself.

430
00:10:03,470 --> 00:10:04,910
I pulled back the curtain.

431
00:10:05,610 --> 00:10:06,347
Parked right

432
00:10:06,347 --> 00:10:07,390
next to my truck,

433
00:10:07,390 --> 00:10:08,741
close enough to touch,

434
00:10:08,741 --> 00:10:10,030
was a green Kenworth.

435
00:10:10,730 --> 00:10:12,295
My father was sitting

436
00:10:12,295 --> 00:10:13,413
in the driver's

437
00:10:13,413 --> 00:10:14,680
seat with his cap

438
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:16,544
pulled down over his eyes

439
00:10:16,544 --> 00:10:18,036
and his arms folded,

440
00:10:18,036 --> 00:10:18,558
asleep.

441
00:10:18,558 --> 00:10:19,738
On his dash were

442
00:10:19,738 --> 00:10:21,066
two cups of coffee

443
00:10:21,066 --> 00:10:22,542
from the truck stop.

444
00:10:22,542 --> 00:10:23,396
One for him.

445
00:10:23,396 --> 00:10:24,179
One for me.

446
00:10:24,179 --> 00:10:25,460
Both of them cold.

447
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,617
He'd hung up the phone

448
00:10:27,617 --> 00:10:29,073
at two in the morning,

449
00:10:29,073 --> 00:10:30,199
put on his boots,

450
00:10:30,199 --> 00:10:31,705
and driven four hundred

451
00:10:31,705 --> 00:10:33,211
miles through the dark.

452
00:10:33,211 --> 00:10:34,195
To a truck stop

453
00:10:34,195 --> 00:10:35,244
he'd never seen.

454
00:10:35,244 --> 00:10:36,033
Because he'd

455
00:10:36,033 --> 00:10:37,150
told me he would.

456
00:10:37,850 --> 00:10:39,272
I knocked on his door.

457
00:10:39,272 --> 00:10:40,481
He opened one eye,

458
00:10:40,481 --> 00:10:41,354
looked at me,

459
00:10:41,354 --> 00:10:42,698
and said, "Sun's up.

460
00:10:42,698 --> 00:10:44,250
You still want to quit?"

461
00:10:44,950 --> 00:10:46,389
I couldn't answer him.

462
00:10:46,389 --> 00:10:47,461
I'd like to tell

463
00:10:47,461 --> 00:10:49,203
you I said something wise.

464
00:10:49,203 --> 00:10:50,016
I didn't say

465
00:10:50,016 --> 00:10:51,100
anything at all.

466
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,901
We had breakfast

467
00:10:52,901 --> 00:10:54,209
in that same booth.

468
00:10:54,209 --> 00:10:55,815
Eggs, sausage, biscuits.

469
00:10:55,815 --> 00:10:57,406
He ate like a man who'd

470
00:10:57,406 --> 00:10:58,998
been driving all night,

471
00:10:58,998 --> 00:10:59,897
which he had.

472
00:10:59,897 --> 00:11:01,352
And when he was done,

473
00:11:01,352 --> 00:11:02,668
he wiped his mouth,

474
00:11:02,668 --> 00:11:04,345
and he told me something

475
00:11:04,345 --> 00:11:05,393
I'd never heard

476
00:11:05,393 --> 00:11:06,790
in twenty-six years.

477
00:11:07,490 --> 00:11:09,037
In nineteen seventy-nine,

478
00:11:09,037 --> 00:11:10,151
the year he bought

479
00:11:10,151 --> 00:11:11,392
that green Kenworth,

480
00:11:11,392 --> 00:11:12,570
he almost quit too.

481
00:11:13,270 --> 00:11:13,964
I was two.

482
00:11:13,964 --> 00:11:15,244
The truck payments

483
00:11:15,244 --> 00:11:16,808
were eating him alive.

484
00:11:16,808 --> 00:11:18,023
He was gone three

485
00:11:18,023 --> 00:11:19,167
weeks at a time.

486
00:11:19,167 --> 00:11:21,021
And one night, he said, at

487
00:11:21,021 --> 00:11:22,804
a truck stop in Arkansas,

488
00:11:22,804 --> 00:11:24,388
he wrote it out on the

489
00:11:24,388 --> 00:11:25,972
back of a fuel receipt

490
00:11:25,972 --> 00:11:27,700
and decided he was done.

491
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:30,180
"I quit about once a month

492
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,961
for three years," he said.

493
00:11:31,961 --> 00:11:32,934
"Always at two

494
00:11:32,934 --> 00:11:33,976
in the morning.

495
00:11:33,976 --> 00:11:35,320
Never once at noon."

496
00:11:36,020 --> 00:11:36,920
Then he reached

497
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:38,060
up to his sun visor

498
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,560
and pulled down a picture

499
00:11:39,560 --> 00:11:40,580
I had never seen.

500
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:42,086
It was me.

501
00:11:42,086 --> 00:11:43,214
Two years old.

502
00:11:43,214 --> 00:11:45,218
In a diaper and a cowboy

503
00:11:45,218 --> 00:11:47,306
hat, sitting on the front

504
00:11:47,306 --> 00:11:49,059
bumper of a brand new

505
00:11:49,059 --> 00:11:50,313
green Kenworth,

506
00:11:50,313 --> 00:11:52,486
crying my eyes out because

507
00:11:52,486 --> 00:11:54,660
I didn't want to get down.

508
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,163
"That's been up

509
00:11:56,163 --> 00:11:57,073
there twenty-four

510
00:11:57,073 --> 00:11:57,930
years," he said.

511
00:11:58,630 --> 00:12:00,453
I didn't know what to say.

512
00:12:00,453 --> 00:12:01,548
I had a picture

513
00:12:01,548 --> 00:12:03,007
of my own boy tucked

514
00:12:03,007 --> 00:12:04,175
in my own visor,

515
00:12:04,175 --> 00:12:05,853
in the exact same spot.

516
00:12:05,853 --> 00:12:06,876
I'd never once

517
00:12:06,876 --> 00:12:08,264
thought about where

518
00:12:08,264 --> 00:12:09,360
I got the idea.

519
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:10,825
Then my father

520
00:12:10,825 --> 00:12:11,862
said the thing I've

521
00:12:11,862 --> 00:12:12,900
carried ever since.

522
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:14,925
"I didn't drive down

523
00:12:14,925 --> 00:12:16,251
here to talk you out

524
00:12:16,251 --> 00:12:17,377
of anything, son.

525
00:12:17,377 --> 00:12:18,849
You want to quit, quit.

526
00:12:18,849 --> 00:12:19,904
You'll be a good

527
00:12:19,904 --> 00:12:21,025
daddy either way.

528
00:12:21,025 --> 00:12:22,283
I came down here so

529
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:23,408
you wouldn't have

530
00:12:23,408 --> 00:12:24,930
to decide by yourself."

531
00:12:25,630 --> 00:12:27,330
I picked up the napkin.

532
00:12:27,330 --> 00:12:29,252
It was still on the table.

533
00:12:29,252 --> 00:12:29,843
Marlene.

534
00:12:29,843 --> 00:12:30,360
I quit.

535
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:30,730
Hank.

536
00:12:31,430 --> 00:12:33,074
He took it out of my hand,

537
00:12:33,074 --> 00:12:34,022
turned it over,

538
00:12:34,022 --> 00:12:35,365
and wrote on the back

539
00:12:35,365 --> 00:12:36,133
with the pen

540
00:12:36,133 --> 00:12:37,540
from the check holder.

541
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:38,302
Then he slid

542
00:12:38,302 --> 00:12:39,190
it back to me.

543
00:12:39,890 --> 00:12:40,499
It said,

544
00:12:40,499 --> 00:12:41,870
Not on a mountain.

545
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:43,777
Not at two in the morning.

546
00:12:43,777 --> 00:12:44,070
Dad.

547
00:12:44,770 --> 00:12:45,853
Then he finished

548
00:12:45,853 --> 00:12:47,546
his coffee, paid for both

549
00:12:47,546 --> 00:12:48,968
of us, and drove four

550
00:12:48,968 --> 00:12:50,254
hundred miles home.

551
00:12:50,254 --> 00:12:51,391
He had a load out

552
00:12:51,391 --> 00:12:52,930
of Columbus that night.

553
00:12:53,630 --> 00:12:54,402
I delivered

554
00:12:54,402 --> 00:12:56,017
my shingles in Atlanta.

555
00:12:56,017 --> 00:12:57,499
Then I called Marlene

556
00:12:57,499 --> 00:12:58,981
and told her I needed

557
00:12:58,981 --> 00:13:00,040
a week at home.

558
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:01,600
She was quiet

559
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,460
for a second.

560
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,097
Then she said, "Hon, I've

561
00:13:04,097 --> 00:13:05,538
been waiting two years

562
00:13:05,538 --> 00:13:07,110
for you to ask me that."

563
00:13:07,810 --> 00:13:08,743
When I pulled

564
00:13:08,743 --> 00:13:09,964
into my driveway,

565
00:13:09,964 --> 00:13:11,472
my boy hid behind his

566
00:13:11,472 --> 00:13:12,402
mother's legs

567
00:13:12,402 --> 00:13:13,762
for about a minute,

568
00:13:13,762 --> 00:13:15,480
like I was somebody new.

569
00:13:15,480 --> 00:13:17,297
Then I took off my old cap

570
00:13:17,297 --> 00:13:18,904
and put it on his head.

571
00:13:18,904 --> 00:13:19,402
It came

572
00:13:19,402 --> 00:13:20,753
down over his eyes.

573
00:13:20,753 --> 00:13:22,373
He wore it for the rest

574
00:13:22,373 --> 00:13:23,218
of the week.

575
00:13:23,218 --> 00:13:24,451
He wore it to bed.

576
00:13:24,451 --> 00:13:25,434
The next year,

577
00:13:25,434 --> 00:13:27,190
he wore it for Halloween.

578
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:29,070
After that week,

579
00:13:29,070 --> 00:13:30,251
I went back out.

580
00:13:30,251 --> 00:13:32,040
Nobody talked me into it.

581
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:33,593
I decided it at noon,

582
00:13:33,593 --> 00:13:35,221
on my own front porch,

583
00:13:35,221 --> 00:13:36,404
with the sun up.

584
00:13:36,404 --> 00:13:37,655
And I didn't miss

585
00:13:37,655 --> 00:13:38,980
his next birthday.

586
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,046
That napkin is still

587
00:13:41,046 --> 00:13:42,345
taped to the inside

588
00:13:42,345 --> 00:13:43,438
of my sun visor,

589
00:13:43,438 --> 00:13:45,214
right next to his picture.

590
00:13:45,214 --> 00:13:46,372
It's been through

591
00:13:46,372 --> 00:13:47,190
four trucks.

592
00:13:47,890 --> 00:13:48,162
Now,

593
00:13:48,162 --> 00:13:49,723
there's one more thing.

594
00:13:49,723 --> 00:13:51,326
And I didn't find it out

595
00:13:51,326 --> 00:13:52,930
until a long time later.

596
00:13:53,630 --> 00:13:55,488
My father passed in March

597
00:13:55,488 --> 00:13:56,975
of two thousand ten.

598
00:13:56,975 --> 00:13:58,283
He was fifty-nine.

599
00:13:58,283 --> 00:14:00,081
After the funeral, I sat

600
00:14:00,081 --> 00:14:01,804
in my mother's kitchen,

601
00:14:01,804 --> 00:14:03,243
at that same table,

602
00:14:03,243 --> 00:14:04,757
and I told her about

603
00:14:04,757 --> 00:14:06,499
the night on Monteagle.

604
00:14:06,499 --> 00:14:07,881
I figured she knew.

605
00:14:07,881 --> 00:14:08,681
She didn't.

606
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:09,806
He'd never told

607
00:14:09,806 --> 00:14:11,080
her a word of it.

608
00:14:11,780 --> 00:14:12,742
But she remembered

609
00:14:12,742 --> 00:14:13,330
that night.

610
00:14:14,030 --> 00:14:15,160
She said she woke

611
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:16,488
up around one-thirty

612
00:14:16,488 --> 00:14:17,485
in the morning,

613
00:14:17,485 --> 00:14:18,276
and his side

614
00:14:18,276 --> 00:14:19,660
of the bed was empty.

615
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:21,034
She found him sitting

616
00:14:21,034 --> 00:14:22,409
at the kitchen table,

617
00:14:22,409 --> 00:14:24,104
dressed, with his boots on

618
00:14:24,104 --> 00:14:25,734
and his keys in his hand.

619
00:14:25,734 --> 00:14:26,982
Just sitting there,

620
00:14:26,982 --> 00:14:27,770
in the dark,

621
00:14:27,770 --> 00:14:29,150
looking at the phone.

622
00:14:29,850 --> 00:14:30,905
She asked him what

623
00:14:30,905 --> 00:14:32,430
in the world he was doing.

624
00:14:33,130 --> 00:14:33,828
And he said,

625
00:14:33,828 --> 00:14:35,340
"Our boy's on a mountain."

626
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:37,295
She said the phone rang

627
00:14:37,295 --> 00:14:38,660
about half an hour later.

628
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,181
I've thought

629
00:14:40,181 --> 00:14:41,344
about that a lot.

630
00:14:41,344 --> 00:14:42,845
I never told him which

631
00:14:42,845 --> 00:14:44,210
mountain I was going

632
00:14:44,210 --> 00:14:45,575
to cross that night.

633
00:14:45,575 --> 00:14:46,595
I hadn't talked

634
00:14:46,595 --> 00:14:47,956
to him in two weeks.

635
00:14:47,956 --> 00:14:49,671
I don't know how he knew,

636
00:14:49,671 --> 00:14:50,563
and my mother

637
00:14:50,563 --> 00:14:51,592
doesn't either.

638
00:14:51,592 --> 00:14:53,311
Maybe a father just knows.

639
00:14:53,311 --> 00:14:54,700
I'd like to think so.

640
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:56,152
Here's what

641
00:14:56,152 --> 00:14:57,246
I know for sure.

642
00:14:57,246 --> 00:14:58,666
My father didn't save

643
00:14:58,666 --> 00:14:59,883
my job that night.

644
00:14:59,883 --> 00:15:01,201
He never even tried.

645
00:15:01,201 --> 00:15:02,832
He showed me what you do

646
00:15:02,832 --> 00:15:04,531
when somebody you love is

647
00:15:04,531 --> 00:15:05,433
at the bottom

648
00:15:05,433 --> 00:15:06,820
of a mountain at two

649
00:15:06,820 --> 00:15:07,860
in the morning.

650
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:09,260
You go.

651
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,742
Last spring, my phone rang

652
00:15:11,742 --> 00:15:13,250
at two in the morning.

653
00:15:13,250 --> 00:15:14,191
It was my boy.

654
00:15:14,191 --> 00:15:15,984
He's twenty-eight now, and

655
00:15:15,984 --> 00:15:17,708
what he was going through

656
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:19,294
is his story, not mine.

657
00:15:19,294 --> 00:15:20,264
He said, "Dad,

658
00:15:20,264 --> 00:15:21,510
I think I'm done."

659
00:15:22,210 --> 00:15:23,105
I said, "Son.

660
00:15:23,105 --> 00:15:24,757
Two in the morning lies.

661
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:25,583
Go to sleep.

662
00:15:25,583 --> 00:15:27,141
If you still feel this

663
00:15:27,141 --> 00:15:28,699
way when the sun's up,

664
00:15:28,699 --> 00:15:30,540
I'll come get you myself."

665
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,008
I was eight

666
00:15:32,008 --> 00:15:33,335
hundred miles away.

667
00:15:33,335 --> 00:15:34,718
I dropped my trailer

668
00:15:34,718 --> 00:15:36,240
and I drove all night.

669
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:38,508
By the time I got there,

670
00:15:38,508 --> 00:15:39,815
he'd already figured

671
00:15:39,815 --> 00:15:40,991
it out on his own.

672
00:15:40,991 --> 00:15:42,067
That's all right.

673
00:15:42,067 --> 00:15:43,650
That was never the point.

674
00:15:44,350 --> 00:15:45,833
If you take one thing

675
00:15:45,833 --> 00:15:47,528
from tonight, take this.

676
00:15:47,528 --> 00:15:48,327
If you ever

677
00:15:48,327 --> 00:15:49,489
drive a mountain

678
00:15:49,489 --> 00:15:50,797
in anything heavy,

679
00:15:50,797 --> 00:15:52,395
a truck, a motor home,

680
00:15:52,395 --> 00:15:54,123
a pickup with a trailer,

681
00:15:54,123 --> 00:15:55,924
pick your gear at the top

682
00:15:55,924 --> 00:15:57,220
and go down slower

683
00:15:57,220 --> 00:15:58,444
than you came up.

684
00:15:58,444 --> 00:16:00,211
If you smell your brakes,

685
00:16:00,211 --> 00:16:01,484
it's already late.

686
00:16:01,484 --> 00:16:02,898
Pull over where it's

687
00:16:02,898 --> 00:16:04,524
safe and let them cool.

688
00:16:04,524 --> 00:16:06,246
And if you see a runaway

689
00:16:06,246 --> 00:16:07,753
ramp and you need it,

690
00:16:07,753 --> 00:16:08,255
use it.

691
00:16:08,255 --> 00:16:08,757
There's

692
00:16:08,757 --> 00:16:10,120
no shame in gravel.

693
00:16:10,820 --> 00:16:11,506
And whatever

694
00:16:11,506 --> 00:16:12,592
mountain you're on,

695
00:16:12,592 --> 00:16:13,792
don't decide anything

696
00:16:13,792 --> 00:16:15,050
at two in the morning.

697
00:16:15,750 --> 00:16:16,502
Next time,

698
00:16:16,502 --> 00:16:18,232
we're going to Montana.

699
00:16:18,232 --> 00:16:20,182
An old man at a truck stop

700
00:16:20,182 --> 00:16:21,833
asked me for a ride to

701
00:16:21,833 --> 00:16:23,633
the house he grew up in.

702
00:16:23,633 --> 00:16:25,001
When we got there,

703
00:16:25,001 --> 00:16:25,913
he handed me

704
00:16:25,913 --> 00:16:27,432
an envelope with ten

705
00:16:27,432 --> 00:16:29,180
thousand dollars in it.

706
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:30,455
And a check dated

707
00:16:30,455 --> 00:16:31,880
nineteen fifty-six.

708
00:16:32,580 --> 00:16:33,592
Before you go,

709
00:16:33,592 --> 00:16:35,399
let me ask you something.

710
00:16:35,399 --> 00:16:37,269
Who showed up for you when

711
00:16:37,269 --> 00:16:38,923
you were ready to quit?

712
00:16:38,923 --> 00:16:40,262
Tell me about them.

713
00:16:40,262 --> 00:16:41,460
I read every one.

714
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,539
Drive safe out there.

715
00:16:43,539 --> 00:16:44,957
And don't quit at two

716
00:16:44,957 --> 00:16:45,970
in the morning.

